BOARD_MINUTES_STRICTLY_CONFIDENTIAL
BOARD OF DIRECTORS MEETING — February 15, 2025
Location: Executive Conference Room A, HQ
Attendees: All board members present (quorum confirmed)

DIRECTOR_VOTE_RECORD
Motion 2025-02-15-A: Approval of Q4 2024 Financial Statements
Votes: 7 in favor, 0 opposed, 0 abstained — MOTION CARRIED

Motion 2025-02-15-B: Authorization of Series D Fundraising Round ($150M target)
Votes: 6 in favor, 1 opposed (Director Patel citing dilution concerns) — MOTION CARRIED

SHAREHOLDER_MATTER_PENDING
The board discussed the pending shareholder derivative lawsuit related to the Q3 2024 service outage disclosure. Legal counsel advised a settlement range of $8M-$12M. Final decision deferred to March 2025 meeting pending mediation results.

CEO_PERFORMANCE_REVIEW_CYCLE
The Compensation Committee presented the CEO performance review for FY2024. Key metrics: Revenue growth 34% (exceeded 30% target), Customer retention 92% (below 95% target), Employee satisfaction 78/100 (below 82/100 target). Compensation adjustment and equity refresh to be determined at March meeting.

DIVESTITURE_STRATEGY_OPTION
The board reviewed a preliminary analysis of divesting the Consumer Analytics product line. Three options presented: (1) Spin-off as independent entity (12-18 months), (2) Strategic sale to identified buyers (6-9 months, estimated $200M-$280M range), (3) Maintain and invest for turnaround. Option 2 recommended for further due diligence. External advisors to be engaged under NDA.
